('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-001','map()','array.map(callback(item, index, array), thisArg)','Creates a new array by calling a function on every element of the original array, without mutating it.','callback — function invoked per element. thisArg — optional value to use as `this` inside callback.','A new array with each element being the result of the callback.','[1, 2, 3].map(x => x * 2); // [2, 4, 6]','javascript','map() always returns a new array of the same length — use filter() first if you want to drop elements.',ARRAY['javascript','array','iteration']::text[],1),
('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-002','filter()','array.filter(callback(item, index, array), thisArg)','Creates a new array containing only the elements that pass a test function.','callback — function invoked per element, should return true to keep the element.','A new array with the elements that passed the test; empty array if none did.','[1, 2, 3, 4].filter(x => x % 2 === 0); // [2, 4]','javascript',null,ARRAY['javascript','array','iteration']::text[],2),
('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-003','reduce()','array.reduce(callback(accumulator, item, index, array), initialValue)','Reduces an array to a single value by applying a function against an accumulator and each element, left to right.','callback — receives the running accumulator and the current element. initialValue — starting value for the accumulator.','The final accumulated value.','[1, 2, 3].reduce((sum, x) => sum + x, 0); // 6','javascript','Without an initialValue, the first array element is used as the initial accumulator and iteration starts from the second element.',ARRAY['javascript','array','iteration']::text[],3),
('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-004','forEach()','array.forEach(callback(item, index, array), thisArg)','Executes a function once for each array element. Used for side effects rather than producing a new value.','callback — function invoked per element. thisArg — optional value to use as `this`.','undefined — forEach() always returns undefined, unlike map().','[1, 2, 3].forEach(x => console.log(x)); // logs 1, 2, 3','javascript','Cannot be stopped early with break; use a for...of loop or some()/every() if you need early exit.',ARRAY['javascript','array','iteration']::text[],4),
('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-005','find()','array.find(callback(item, index, array), thisArg)','Returns the first element in the array that satisfies the provided test function.','callback — function invoked per element until it returns truthy.','The first matching element, or undefined if none match.','[5, 12, 8].find(x => x > 10); // 12','javascript','Stops iterating as soon as a match is found, unlike filter() which checks every element.',ARRAY['javascript','array','search']::text[],5),
