('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-014','shift()','array.shift()','Removes the first element from an array and returns it, mutating the original array and shifting remaining elements down.',null,'The removed element, or undefined if the array was empty.','const a = [1, 2, 3]; a.shift(); // 1, a is [2, 3]','javascript','O(n) operation since every remaining element must be re-indexed — avoid in hot loops on large arrays.',ARRAY['javascript','array','mutation']::text[],14),
