('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-016','splice()','array.splice(start, deleteCount, item1, item2, ...)','Changes the contents of an array by removing, replacing, or adding elements in place.','start — index to begin changing. deleteCount — number of elements to remove. item1... — elements to insert.','An array containing the deleted elements.','const a = [1, 2, 3, 4]; a.splice(1, 2, ''x''); // a is [1, ''x'', 4]','javascript','Mutates the original array — use slice() if you need a non-mutating alternative.',ARRAY['javascript','array','mutation']::text[],16),
('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-017','slice()','array.slice(start, end)','Returns a shallow copy of a portion of an array, from start up to (but not including) end, without mutating the original.','start — index to begin extraction (default 0). end — index to stop before (default array length).','A new array containing the extracted elements.','[1, 2, 3, 4].slice(1, 3); // [2, 3]','javascript','Negative indices count from the end of the array.',ARRAY['javascript','array','copy']::text[],17),
('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-018','concat()','array.concat(array2, array3, ...)','Merges two or more arrays into a new array, without mutating any of the originals.','array2, array3, ... — arrays or values to merge in.','A new array combining all the elements.','[1, 2].concat([3, 4], [5]); // [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]','javascript','The spread operator ([...a, ...b]) is a commonly used alternative for merging arrays.',ARRAY['javascript','array','copy']::text[],18),
