('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-020','sort()','array.sort(compareFn)','Sorts the elements of an array in place according to a compare function, or as strings by default.','compareFn — optional function (a, b) => number; negative sorts a first, positive sorts b first.','The same array, sorted in place.','[10, 1, 21].sort((a, b) => a - b); // [1, 10, 21]','javascript','Without a compareFn, elements are converted to strings and sorted lexicographically — [10, 1, 21].sort() gives [1, 10, 21] wrong; always pass a compareFn for numbers.',ARRAY['javascript','array','mutation']::text[],20),
('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-021','reverse()','array.reverse()','Reverses the order of the elements of an array in place.',null,'The same array, with elements reversed.','[1, 2, 3].reverse(); // [3, 2, 1]','javascript','Mutates the original array — use [...array].reverse() to avoid mutating.',ARRAY['javascript','array','mutation']::text[],21),
('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-022','flat()','array.flat(depth)','Creates a new array with all sub-array elements concatenated into it up to the specified depth.','depth — how deep to flatten nested arrays (default 1). Use Infinity to flatten fully.','A new, flattened array.','[1, [2, [3, 4]]].flat(2); // [1, 2, 3, 4]','javascript',null,ARRAY['javascript','array','iteration']::text[],22),
