('javascript','array-methods','javascript-array-methods-024','Array.from()','Array.from(arrayLike, mapFn)','Creates a new array instance from an array-like or iterable object, such as a NodeList, string, or Set.','arrayLike — object with a length property or an iterable. mapFn — optional function applied to each element.','A new Array instance.','Array.from({ length: 3 }, (_, i) => i * 2); // [0, 2, 4]','javascript','Commonly used to convert NodeLists, Sets, or Maps into real arrays so array methods can be used.',ARRAY['javascript','array','conversion']::text[],24),
