('javascript','es6-plus','javascript-es6-plus-001','let','let variableName = value;','Declares a block-scoped variable that can be reassigned but not redeclared in the same scope.',null,null,'let count = 1; count = 2; // ok','javascript','Unlike var, let is not hoisted to a usable state — accessing it before declaration throws a ReferenceError (the "temporal dead zone").',ARRAY['javascript','es6','variables']::text[],1),
