('javascript','string-methods','javascript-string-methods-022','String.concat()','string.concat(str2, str3, ...)','Combines the text of one or more strings and returns a new string.','str2, str3, ... — strings to concatenate.','A new string combining all inputs.','''Hello, ''.concat(''World'', ''!''); // ''Hello, World!''','javascript','Template literals or the + operator are generally preferred over concat() in modern code.',ARRAY['javascript','string','formatting']::text[],22),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-001','var vs let vs const','var x; let y; const z = 1;','The three ways to declare a variable in JavaScript: var is function-scoped and hoisted, while let and const are block-scoped and cannot be redeclared in the same scope.',null,null,'if (true) { var a = 1; let b = 2; } console.log(a); // 1, b is not defined here','javascript','Modern code generally avoids var in favor of let (for reassignable values) and const (the default choice).',ARRAY['javascript','variables','scope']::text[],1),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-002','Primitive Data Types',null,'JavaScript has seven primitive types: string, number, boolean, undefined, null, bigint, and symbol. Primitives are immutable and compared by value.',null,null,'typeof ''hi''; // ''string''
typeof 42; // ''number''
typeof true; // ''boolean''','javascript','typeof null returns ''object'' — a long-standing quirk of the language, not a sign that null is a reference type.',ARRAY['javascript','data-types','primitives']::text[],2),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-003','Reference Types (Objects)',null,'Non-primitive values — objects, arrays, and functions — are reference types. Variables holding them store a reference to the value in memory, not the value itself.',null,null,'const a = { x: 1 }; const b = a; b.x = 2; console.log(a.x); // 2, same object','javascript','Assigning or passing an object copies the reference, not the data — use spread or structuredClone() to copy the actual contents.',ARRAY['javascript','data-types','objects']::text[],3),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-004','Type Coercion',null,'JavaScript''s automatic or implicit conversion of values from one data type to another, such as during comparisons or arithmetic with mixed types.',null,null,'''5'' + 1; // ''51'' (number coerced to string)
''5'' - 1; // 4 (string coerced to number)','javascript','Use === instead of == to avoid unexpected coercion during comparisons.',ARRAY['javascript','data-types','coercion']::text[],4),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-005','Truthy and Falsy Values',null,'In boolean contexts, every value is either truthy or falsy. The falsy values are false, 0, -0, '''', null, undefined, and NaN — everything else is truthy.',null,null,'if ('''') { } // does not run, '''' is falsy
if (''0'') { } // runs, non-empty string is truthy','javascript','An empty array [] and empty object {} are both truthy, which surprises many developers coming from other languages.',ARRAY['javascript','data-types','conditionals']::text[],5),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-006','NaN',null,'"Not a Number" — a special numeric value representing the result of an invalid or undefined mathematical operation.',null,null,'0 / 0; // NaN
NaN === NaN; // false','javascript','Use Number.isNaN(value) rather than isNaN(value) to avoid unwanted type coercion of non-numeric input.',ARRAY['javascript','data-types','numbers']::text[],6),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-007','undefined vs null',null,'undefined means a variable has been declared but not assigned a value; null is an explicit assignment representing "no value" or "empty", set intentionally by a developer.',null,null,'let a; console.log(a); // undefined
let b = null; console.log(b); // null','javascript','undefined == null is true, but undefined === null is false — they are distinct types.',ARRAY['javascript','data-types','null']::text[],7),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-008','Dynamic Typing',null,'JavaScript variables are not bound to a specific type; the same variable can hold a string, then a number, then an object, over its lifetime.',null,null,'let x = ''hello''; x = 42; x = { a: 1 }; // all valid','javascript','TypeScript adds static typing on top of JavaScript''s dynamic typing to catch these kinds of mismatches at compile time.',ARRAY['javascript','data-types','typing']::text[],8),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-009','Number Precision (Floating Point)',null,'JavaScript represents all numbers as 64-bit floating point (IEEE 754), which can cause small rounding errors in decimal arithmetic.',null,null,'0.1 + 0.2; // 0.30000000000000004','javascript','For exact decimal math (e.g. currency), round with toFixed(), scale to integers, or use a dedicated decimal library.',ARRAY['javascript','numbers','precision']::text[],9),
('javascript','variables-data-types','javascript-variables-data-types-010','Global Scope',null,'Variables and functions declared outside any function or block live in the global scope and are accessible from anywhere in the program.',null,null,'var globalVar = ''I am global''; function show() { console.log(globalVar); }','javascript','Excessive use of global scope increases the risk of naming collisions — ES modules scope top-level declarations to the module instead.',ARRAY['javascript','variables','scope']::text[],10),
('html','attributes','html-attributes-001','id','<div id="unique-name">','Assigns a unique identifier to an element, used to target it from CSS, JavaScript or an in-page anchor link.',null,null,'<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
<a href="#contact">Jump to Contact</a>','html','Must be unique within the page — duplicate ids break getElementById and CSS specificity assumptions.',ARRAY['html','attribute','css']::text[],1),
('html','attributes','html-attributes-002','class','<div class="card highlight">','Assigns one or more space-separated class names to an element for styling with CSS or selection with JavaScript.',null,null,'<button class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>','html','Unlike id, class is not unique — many elements can share the same class.',ARRAY['html','attribute','css']::text[],2),
('html','attributes','html-attributes-003','style','<div style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">','Applies inline CSS declarations directly to a single element.',null,null,'<p style="color: blue; margin: 0;">Inline styled text</p>','html','Inline styles have very high specificity and are hard to override — prefer classes for anything reused.',ARRAY['html','attribute','css']::text[],3),
('html','attributes','html-attributes-004','src','<img src="path/to/file" />','Specifies the URL of an external resource to embed, used on elements like <img>, <script>, <video>, <audio> and <iframe>.',null,null,'<script src="/js/app.js"></script>','html',null,ARRAY['html','attribute','media']::text[],4),
('html','attributes','html-attributes-005','href','<a href="https://example.com">','Specifies the destination URL for a hyperlink or linked resource, used on <a> and <link>.',null,null,'<a href="/about">About us</a>','html','A href starting with # links to an element with a matching id on the same page.',ARRAY['html','attribute','navigation']::text[],5),
('html','attributes','html-attributes-006','alt','<img alt="description" />','Provides alternative text for an image, read by screen readers and shown if the image fails to load.',null,null,'<img src="cat.jpg" alt="A orange tabby cat sleeping" />','html','Use alt="" (empty) for purely decorative images so screen readers skip them.',ARRAY['html','attribute','accessibility']::text[],6),
('html','attributes','html-attributes-007','title','<abbr title="...">','Provides advisory, supplementary text for an element, typically shown as a tooltip on hover.',null,null,'<span title="Coordinated Universal Time">UTC</span>','html','Not reliably accessible (not announced on focus by all screen readers) — don''t rely on it as the sole source of critical information.',ARRAY['html','attribute','accessibility']::text[],7),
