('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-010','<input type="range">','<input type="range" min="0" max="100" />','A slider control for picking a numeric value within a range, when the exact number matters less than a rough position.','min, max — range bounds. step — increment size.',null,'<input type="range" min="0" max="100" step="10" value="50" />','html','Doesn''t show its current value visually — pair it with an output element or JS listener to display it.',ARRAY['html','forms','input']::text[],10),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-011','<input type="color">','<input type="color" value="#ff0000" />','Opens a native color picker and returns the selected color as a hex string.',null,null,'<input type="color" name="theme" value="#3366ff" />','html','Always returns a 6-digit hex value, never supports alpha transparency.',ARRAY['html','forms','input']::text[],11),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-012','<label>','<label for="id">Text</label>','Provides a caption for a form control, improving accessibility and letting a click on the label focus the associated control.','for — id of the associated form control (or wrap the control directly inside the label instead).',null,'<label for="email">Email</label>
<input id="email" type="email" />','html','Every form control should have an associated label — placeholder text alone isn''t accessible enough.',ARRAY['html','forms','accessibility']::text[],12),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-013','<select>','<select name="..."><option>...</option></select>','A dropdown control for choosing one (or, with multiple, several) values from a predefined list of <option> elements.','multiple — allows selecting more than one option. size — number of visible rows.',null,'<select name="country">
  <option value="us">United States</option>
  <option value="in">India</option>
</select>','html',null,ARRAY['html','forms','input']::text[],13),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-014','<option>','<option value="val">Label</option>','Defines a single choice within a <select> dropdown or a <datalist>.','value — value submitted when selected. selected — pre-selects this option.',null,'<option value="in" selected>India</option>','html','If value is omitted, the option''s text content is used as the submitted value.',ARRAY['html','forms']::text[],14),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-015','<textarea>','<textarea rows="4" cols="30">text</textarea>','A multi-line, resizable free text input field.','rows/cols — visible size. maxlength — max character count.',null,'<textarea name="bio" rows="4" placeholder="Tell us about yourself"></textarea>','html','Unlike <input>, its default value is set via inner text content, not a value attribute.',ARRAY['html','forms','input']::text[],15),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-016','<button>','<button type="submit">Save</button>','A clickable control that can submit a form, reset it, or trigger custom JavaScript, depending on its type.','type — submit (default inside a form), reset, or button (no default action).',null,'<button type="button" onclick="doThing()">Click me</button>','html','Inside a <form>, a button defaults to type="submit" — set type="button" explicitly to avoid accidental submits.',ARRAY['html','forms','javascript']::text[],16),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-017','<fieldset>','<fieldset>...</fieldset>','Groups a set of related form controls together, typically rendered with a surrounding border.','disabled — disables every control nested inside it at once.',null,'<fieldset>
  <legend>Shipping address</legend>
  <input type="text" name="street" />
</fieldset>','html',null,ARRAY['html','forms','accessibility']::text[],17),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-018','<legend>','<fieldset><legend>Title</legend>...</fieldset>','Provides a caption for the contents of an enclosing <fieldset>.',null,null,'<legend>Payment details</legend>','html','Must be the first child of <fieldset>.',ARRAY['html','forms','accessibility']::text[],18),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-019','required','<input required />','Marks a form control as mandatory, blocking form submission and showing a browser validation message until it''s filled in.',null,null,'<input type="text" name="name" required />','html','Client-side only — always re-validate required fields on the server too.',ARRAY['html','forms','validation']::text[],19),
('html','forms-inputs','html-forms-inputs-020','pattern','<input pattern="[0-9]{5}" />','Restricts a text-like input''s valid value to one matching a given regular expression.','A JavaScript-flavored regex, without surrounding slashes.',null,'<input type="text" pattern="[0-9]{5}" title="5-digit ZIP code" />','html','Pair it with title so the browser''s default validation message explains the expected format.',ARRAY['html','forms','validation']::text[],20),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-001','<header>','<header>...</header>','Represents introductory content for its nearest ancestor — page title and nav for the page, or a heading/byline for an <article>.',null,null,'<header>
  <h1>My Blog</h1>
  <nav>...</nav>
</header>','html','Unlike a <div class="header">, screen readers can jump straight to it as a landmark region.',ARRAY['html','semantic','landmark']::text[],1),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-002','<nav>','<nav>...</nav>','Marks a block of major navigation links, such as a site''s main menu or breadcrumbs.',null,null,'<nav>
  <a href="/">Home</a>
  <a href="/about">About</a>
</nav>','html','Reserve it for primary navigation blocks — not every group of links needs to be a <nav>.',ARRAY['html','semantic','landmark']::text[],2),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-003','<main>','<main>...</main>','Identifies the dominant, unique content of the document, excluding repeated elements like headers, footers and sidebars.',null,null,'<main>
  <h1>Article title</h1>
  <p>Content...</p>
</main>','html','Should appear exactly once per page and lets screen reader users skip straight to the primary content.',ARRAY['html','semantic','landmark']::text[],3),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-004','<article>','<article>...</article>','Represents a self-contained piece of content that would make sense distributed or syndicated on its own, like a blog post, news story or forum comment.',null,null,'<article>
  <h2>Post title</h2>
  <p>Post body...</p>
</article>','html','The test: if you could pull this out and reuse it elsewhere and it would still make sense, it''s an <article>.',ARRAY['html','semantic','block']::text[],4),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-005','<section>','<section>...</section>','Groups a thematically related chunk of content, typically with its own heading, that forms a distinct part of the page.',null,null,'<section>
  <h2>Reviews</h2>
  <p>...</p>
</section>','html','Unlike <div>, a <section> implies the content is a distinct, headed thematic group — not just a styling wrapper.',ARRAY['html','semantic','block']::text[],5),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-006','<aside>','<aside>...</aside>','Represents content tangentially related to the surrounding content, such as a sidebar, pull quote or ad block.',null,null,'<aside>
  <h3>Related posts</h3>
  <ul>...</ul>
</aside>','html','Content could be removed without reducing the meaning of the main content around it.',ARRAY['html','semantic','block']::text[],6),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-007','<footer>','<footer>...</footer>','Represents footer content for its nearest ancestor — copyright, contact links or related documents for the page, or metadata for an <article>.',null,null,'<footer>
  <p>&copy; 2026 My Company</p>
</footer>','html',null,ARRAY['html','semantic','landmark']::text[],7),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-008','<figure>','<figure><img /><figcaption>...</figcaption></figure>','Groups self-contained content — usually an image, diagram or code snippet — together with an optional caption, as a single referenceable unit.',null,null,'<figure>
  <img src="chart.png" alt="Sales chart" />
  <figcaption>Fig 1. Quarterly sales</figcaption>
</figure>','html','Semantically ties an image to its caption, unlike a plain <div> wrapping an <img> and a <p>.',ARRAY['html','semantic','media']::text[],8),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-009','<figcaption>','<figure>...<figcaption>caption</figcaption></figure>','Provides a caption or legend describing the contents of its parent <figure>.',null,null,'<figcaption>A diagram of the request lifecycle.</figcaption>','html','Can appear as the first or last child of <figure>.',ARRAY['html','semantic','media']::text[],9),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-010','<time>','<time datetime="2026-09-18">Sept 18, 2026</time>','Marks up a human-readable date or time while also providing a machine-readable equivalent for browsers and search engines.','datetime — the machine-readable ISO 8601 value.',null,'<time datetime="2026-09-18T10:00">10am on September 18</time>','html','Unlike a plain <span>, it lets tools reliably parse and index the date regardless of how it''s displayed.',ARRAY['html','semantic','inline']::text[],10),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-011','<mark>','<mark>highlighted text</mark>','Highlights text that is relevant or noteworthy in the current context, such as a search term match.',null,null,'<p>Results for <mark>react hooks</mark> found 12 matches.</p>','html','Conveys relevance, unlike <span class="highlight"> which carries no meaning without CSS.',ARRAY['html','semantic','inline']::text[],11),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-012','<address>','<address>...</address>','Provides contact information for the nearest <article> or the page''s author/owner — a person, organization or email, not a postal address specifically.',null,null,'<address>
  Written by <a href="mailto:jane@example.com">Jane Doe</a>
</address>','html','Despite the name, it''s for authorship/contact info, not for marking up arbitrary street addresses.',ARRAY['html','semantic','block']::text[],12),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-013','<details>','<details><summary>Title</summary>content</details>','Creates a native, collapsible disclosure widget that the user can toggle open or closed, with no JavaScript required.','open — pre-expands the widget.',null,'<details>
  <summary>More info</summary>
  <p>Hidden content revealed on click.</p>
</details>','html','Replaces the common pattern of a button plus JS-toggled div for simple show/hide UI.',ARRAY['html','semantic','ui']::text[],13),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-014','<summary>','<details><summary>label</summary>...</details>','Defines the always-visible label/heading for a <details> disclosure widget; clicking it toggles the widget open or closed.',null,null,'<summary>Click to expand</summary>','html','Must be the first child of <details>; only one <summary> is used per <details>.',ARRAY['html','semantic','ui']::text[],14),
('html','semantic-tags','html-semantic-tags-015','<search>','<search>...</search>','Identifies a section containing search or filtering controls for the current page or site, as a distinct landmark region.',null,null,'<search>
  <form action="/search">
    <input type="search" name="q" />
  </form>
</search>','html','A newer semantic landmark — before it existed, a <form role="search"> was the common substitute.',ARRAY['html','semantic','landmark']::text[],15),
('html','tags','html-tags-001','<html>','<html lang="en">...</html>','The root element of an HTML document; every other element is nested inside it.','lang — declares the document''s language for accessibility tools and search engines.',null,'<html lang="en">
  <head></head>
  <body></body>
</html>','html',null,ARRAY['html','document-structure','root']::text[],1),
('html','tags','html-tags-002','<head>','<head>...</head>','Container for machine-readable metadata about the document — title, character set, styles, scripts — that isn''t rendered on the page itself.',null,null,'<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>My Page</title>
</head>','html',null,ARRAY['html','document-structure','metadata']::text[],2),
('html','tags','html-tags-003','<body>','<body>...</body>','Contains all the visible content of an HTML document — text, images, links and every other rendered element.',null,null,'<body>
  <h1>Welcome</h1>
</body>','html','A document can only have one <body>.',ARRAY['html','document-structure']::text[],3),
('html','tags','html-tags-004','<title>','<title>Page Title</title>','Sets the document''s title, shown in the browser tab, bookmarks and search engine results.',null,null,'<title>My Portfolio</title>','html','Must be placed inside <head>; each document should have exactly one <title>.',ARRAY['html','metadata','seo']::text[],4),
('html','tags','html-tags-005','<meta>','<meta name="..." content="..." />','Defines metadata such as character encoding, viewport settings, author or SEO description that isn''t represented by other head elements.','charset — document encoding. name/content — key-value metadata pair. viewport — controls responsive scaling on mobile.',null,'<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />','html','A self-closing, void element — it has no closing tag or children.',ARRAY['html','metadata','seo']::text[],5),
('html','tags','html-tags-006','<link>','<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />','Links an external resource — most commonly a CSS stylesheet, but also favicons, preloads and fonts — to the document.','rel — relationship to the document (e.g. stylesheet, icon, preload). href — URL of the resource.',null,'<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css" />
<link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico" />','html','Void element; belongs in <head>.',ARRAY['html','metadata','css']::text[],6),
('html','tags','html-tags-007','<script>','<script src="app.js"></script>','Embeds or references JavaScript that runs in the page, either inline or via an external file.','src — path to an external script. defer — runs the script after HTML parsing. async — runs it as soon as it''s downloaded, without blocking parsing.',null,'<script src="app.js" defer></script>','html','A script without defer/async blocks HTML parsing at the point it appears, which is why scripts are often placed before </body>.',ARRAY['html','javascript','document-structure']::text[],7),
('html','tags','html-tags-008','<style>','<style>...</style>','Embeds CSS rules directly inside the document rather than linking an external stylesheet.',null,null,'<style>
  body { margin: 0; }
</style>','html','Best used for small, page-specific styles; prefer <link> for shared stylesheets.',ARRAY['html','css','document-structure']::text[],8),
('html','tags','html-tags-009','<p>','<p>Text</p>','Represents a paragraph of text — a self-contained block of related content.',null,null,'<p>This is a paragraph of text.</p>','html',null,ARRAY['html','text-content','block']::text[],9),
('html','tags','html-tags-010','<h1>–<h6>','<h1>Heading</h1>','Six levels of section headings, <h1> being the most important and <h6> the least, used to structure a document''s outline.',null,null,'<h1>Main Title</h1>
<h2>Subsection</h2>','html','Use heading levels in order for accessibility and SEO — don''t skip levels purely for visual size (use CSS for that instead).',ARRAY['html','text-content','accessibility']::text[],10),
('html','tags','html-tags-011','<a>','<a href="url">link text</a>','Creates a hyperlink to another page, a location within the page, a file or an email/phone address.','href — destination URL. target — where to open it (e.g. _blank). rel — relationship, such as noopener for security on external links.',null,'<a href="https://example.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit site</a>','html','Use rel="noopener noreferrer" with target="_blank" to prevent the new page from accessing window.opener.',ARRAY['html','text-content','navigation']::text[],11),
('html','tags','html-tags-012','<span>','<span>text</span>','A generic inline container with no semantic meaning, used to style or script a piece of text.',null,null,'<p>This is <span class="highlight">important</span>.</p>','html','Prefer a semantic inline element (like <strong> or <time>) over <span> when one fits the meaning.',ARRAY['html','text-content','generic']::text[],12),
('html','tags','html-tags-013','<div>','<div>content</div>','A generic block-level container with no semantic meaning, used for grouping elements for styling or scripting.',null,null,'<div class="card">
  <p>Card content</p>
</div>','html','Prefer a semantic element (<section>, <article>, <nav>, etc.) over <div> when the content has meaning.',ARRAY['html','block','generic']::text[],13),
('html','tags','html-tags-014','<br>','text<br />more text','Inserts a single line break within text, such as in an address or poem.',null,null,'123 Main St<br />Springfield','html','Void element. Don''t use it to add spacing between block elements — use CSS margin instead.',ARRAY['html','text-content']::text[],14),
('html','tags','html-tags-015','<hr>','<hr />','Represents a thematic break between paragraphs or sections, typically rendered as a horizontal line.',null,null,'<p>Section one.</p>
<hr />
<p>Section two.</p>','html','Void element.',ARRAY['html','text-content','block']::text[],15),
('html','tags','html-tags-016','<strong>','<strong>text</strong>','Marks text as having strong importance, seriousness or urgency; browsers render it bold by default.',null,null,'<p><strong>Warning:</strong> this action cannot be undone.</p>','html','Semantic — conveys importance to screen readers, unlike <b> which is purely visual.',ARRAY['html','text-content','inline']::text[],16),
('html','tags','html-tags-017','<em>','<em>text</em>','Marks text with stressed emphasis, typically changing the meaning of the sentence; browsers render it italic by default.',null,null,'<p>I <em>really</em> mean it.</p>','html','Semantic emphasis, as opposed to <i> which is purely visual italics.',ARRAY['html','text-content','inline']::text[],17),
('html','tags','html-tags-018','<b>','<b>text</b>','Draws visual attention to text (bold) without implying extra importance — a stylistic offset, not a semantic one.',null,null,'<p>The <b>keyword</b> in this recipe is optional.</p>','html','Use <strong> instead when the text is actually important, not just visually bold.',ARRAY['html','text-content','inline']::text[],18),
('html','tags','html-tags-019','<i>','<i>text</i>','Represents text in an alternate voice or mood, such as a technical term, foreign phrase or ship name — rendered italic.',null,null,'<p>The term <i>hoisting</i> refers to variable declarations.</p>','html','Use <em> instead when the text carries actual emphasis rather than just an alternate tone.',ARRAY['html','text-content','inline']::text[],19),
('html','tags','html-tags-020','<sub>','<sub>text</sub>','Renders text as subscript, lower and smaller than the surrounding text — commonly used in chemical formulas or footnotes.',null,null,'H<sub>2</sub>O','html',null,ARRAY['html','text-content','inline']::text[],20),
('html','tags','html-tags-021','<sup>','<sup>text</sup>','Renders text as superscript, raised and smaller than the surrounding text — commonly used for exponents or ordinal suffixes.',null,null,'x<sup>2</sup> + 1','html',null,ARRAY['html','text-content','inline']::text[],21),
('html','tags','html-tags-022','<abbr>','<abbr title="...">ABBR</abbr>','Marks up an abbreviation or acronym, optionally providing its full expansion via the title attribute.','title — the full expansion, shown as a tooltip on hover.',null,'<abbr title="HyperText Markup Language">HTML</abbr>','html',null,ARRAY['html','text-content','accessibility']::text[],22),
('html','tags','html-tags-023','<q>','<q>quoted text</q>','Marks a short, inline quotation; browsers typically wrap the content in quotation marks automatically.','cite — optional URL of the quote''s source.',null,'She said <q>this changes everything</q>.','html','Use <blockquote> instead for longer, block-level quotations.',ARRAY['html','text-content','inline']::text[],23),
('html','tags','html-tags-024','<blockquote>','<blockquote cite="url">...</blockquote>','Represents an extended quotation set off from the surrounding text as its own block.','cite — optional URL identifying the source of the quotation.',null,'<blockquote cite="https://example.com">
  <p>The best code is no code at all.</p>
</blockquote>','html',null,ARRAY['html','text-content','block']::text[],24),
('html','tags','html-tags-025','<pre>','<pre>  preformatted
  text</pre>','Preserves whitespace and line breaks exactly as written, rendering the content in a monospace font.',null,null,'<pre>
function add(a, b) {
  return a + b;
}
</pre>','html','Commonly wraps a <code> element for displaying code blocks.',ARRAY['html','text-content','block']::text[],25),
('html','tags','html-tags-026','<code>','<code>inline code</code>','Marks up a short fragment of computer code, rendered in a monospace font.',null,null,'Use the <code>Array.map()</code> method.','html','Wrap in <pre> to preserve formatting for multi-line code blocks.',ARRAY['html','text-content','inline']::text[],26),
('html','tags','html-tags-027','<ul>','<ul><li>item</li></ul>','Groups a set of items into an unordered (bulleted) list.',null,null,'<ul>
  <li>Milk</li>
  <li>Eggs</li>
</ul>','html',null,ARRAY['html','list','block']::text[],27),
('html','tags','html-tags-028','<ol>','<ol><li>item</li></ol>','Groups a set of items into an ordered (numbered) list.','start — the number to begin counting from. reversed — counts down instead of up.',null,'<ol start="3">
  <li>Third</li>
  <li>Fourth</li>
</ol>','html',null,ARRAY['html','list','block']::text[],28),
('html','tags','html-tags-029','<li>','<li>item</li>','Represents a single item within a <ul>, <ol> or <menu> list.','value — overrides the item''s number, only meaningful inside an <ol>.',null,'<ul>
  <li>First item</li>
</ul>','html',null,ARRAY['html','list']::text[],29),
('html','tags','html-tags-030','<dl>','<dl><dt>term</dt><dd>def</dd></dl>','A description list that pairs terms with their descriptions, such as a glossary or metadata list.',null,null,'<dl>
  <dt>HTML</dt>
  <dd>The markup language of the web.</dd>
</dl>','html',null,ARRAY['html','list','block']::text[],30),
('html','tags','html-tags-031','<dt>','<dt>term</dt>','Defines a term or name inside a <dl> description list.',null,null,'<dt>API</dt>','html','Must be followed by one or more <dd> elements.',ARRAY['html','list']::text[],31),
('html','tags','html-tags-032','<dd>','<dd>description</dd>','Provides the description or value for the preceding <dt> term inside a <dl> list.',null,null,'<dd>Application Programming Interface</dd>','html',null,ARRAY['html','list']::text[],32),
('html','tags','html-tags-033','<table>','<table>...</table>','Represents tabular data organized into rows and columns.',null,null,'<table>
  <tr><td>1</td><td>2</td></tr>
</table>','html','Use tables for actual tabular data, not for page layout.',ARRAY['html','table','block']::text[],33),
('html','tags','html-tags-034','<thead>','<thead><tr><th>...</th></tr></thead>','Groups the header row(s) of a table, separating column labels from the body data.',null,null,'<thead>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Age</th></tr>
</thead>','html',null,ARRAY['html','table']::text[],34),
('html','tags','html-tags-035','<tbody>','<tbody><tr><td>...</td></tr></tbody>','Groups the main body rows of a table, distinct from its header and footer.',null,null,'<tbody>
  <tr><td>Alice</td><td>30</td></tr>
</tbody>','html',null,ARRAY['html','table']::text[],35),
('html','tags','html-tags-036','<tr>','<tr><td>...</td></tr>','Represents a single row of cells within a table.',null,null,'<tr>
  <td>Row 1, Cell 1</td>
  <td>Row 1, Cell 2</td>
</tr>','html',null,ARRAY['html','table']::text[],36),
('html','tags','html-tags-037','<th>','<th scope="col">Header</th>','Defines a header cell in a table, labeling a row or column; rendered bold and centered by default.','scope — indicates whether the header applies to a row or column, improving screen-reader table navigation.',null,'<th scope="col">Name</th>','html',null,ARRAY['html','table','accessibility']::text[],37),
('html','tags','html-tags-038','<td>','<td>data</td>','Defines a standard data cell within a table row.','colspan — number of columns to span. rowspan — number of rows to span.',null,'<td colspan="2">Spans two columns</td>','html',null,ARRAY['html','table']::text[],38),
('html','tags','html-tags-039','<caption>','<table><caption>Title</caption>...</table>','Provides a title or explanation for a table, announced by screen readers before the table content.',null,null,'<table>
  <caption>Monthly Sales</caption>
  <tr><td>...</td></tr>
</table>','html','Must be the first child of <table>.',ARRAY['html','table','accessibility']::text[],39),
('html','tags','html-tags-040','<img>','<img src="pic.jpg" alt="description" />','Embeds an image into the document.','src — image URL. alt — alternative text for accessibility and when the image fails to load. width/height — intrinsic dimensions to avoid layout shift.',null,'<img src="logo.png" alt="Company logo" width="200" height="100" />','html','Void element. Always provide alt text (empty alt="" for purely decorative images).',ARRAY['html','media']::text[],40),
('html','tags','html-tags-041','<video>','<video src="movie.mp4" controls></video>','Embeds a video player, optionally with playback controls and multiple source fallbacks.','controls — shows the native player UI. autoplay, loop, muted — playback behavior. poster — preview image before playback.',null,'<video controls width="400">
  <source src="movie.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
</video>','html','Browsers block autoplay with sound unless muted is also set.',ARRAY['html','media']::text[],41),
('html','tags','html-tags-042','<audio>','<audio src="song.mp3" controls></audio>','Embeds an audio player for playing sound or music files.','controls — shows native playback controls. autoplay, loop, muted — playback behavior.',null,'<audio controls>
  <source src="song.mp3" type="audio/mpeg" />
</audio>','html',null,ARRAY['html','media']::text[],42),
('html','tags','html-tags-043','<source>','<source src="file.webm" type="video/webm" />','Specifies an alternate media resource for <video>, <audio> or <picture>, letting the browser pick the best supported format.','src/srcset — resource URL. type — MIME type. media — condition for <picture> sources.',null,'<video>
  <source src="movie.webm" type="video/webm" />
  <source src="movie.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
</video>','html','Void element; the browser uses the first <source> it supports.',ARRAY['html','media']::text[],43),
('html','tags','html-tags-044','<picture>','<picture><source .../><img .../></picture>','Wraps multiple <source> candidates and a fallback <img>, letting the browser choose the best image for the screen size or format.',null,null,'<picture>
  <source srcset="large.jpg" media="(min-width: 800px)" />
  <img src="small.jpg" alt="Landscape" />
</picture>','html','Used for art direction and serving next-gen image formats with fallbacks.',ARRAY['html','media','responsive']::text[],44),
('html','tags','html-tags-045','<track>','<track src="subs.vtt" kind="subtitles" srclang="en" />','Adds timed text tracks — subtitles, captions or descriptions — to a <video> or <audio> element.','kind — subtitles, captions, descriptions, chapters. src — WebVTT file URL. srclang — language code.',null,'<video controls>
