('dom','common-apis','dom-common-apis-010','ResizeObserver vs window resize event',null,'The window ''resize'' event only fires when the entire browser viewport changes, while ResizeObserver detects size changes of any individual element regardless of cause (e.g. content change, flex layout shifts).',null,null,null,'javascript','Prefer ResizeObserver when you need to react to a specific element''s size rather than the whole window.',ARRAY['dom','observers','layout']::text[],10),
('dom','events','dom-events-001','addEventListener()','target.addEventListener(type, listener, options)','Registers a function to be called whenever the specified event fires on the target.','type — event name, e.g. ''click''. listener — the callback function. options — optional object with capture, once, passive, signal.','undefined.','button.addEventListener(''click'', () => console.log(''clicked''));','javascript','Multiple listeners can be attached to the same event without overwriting each other, unlike onclick assignment.',ARRAY['dom','events']::text[],1),
